IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `vmu-nouns`
IMPORT `vmu-time`

-- Sections 4 and 5: the meaning of a fee unit, and how the value of a fee unit or a penalty unit and the annual rate come about.
-- A value fixed by the Treasurer for a financial year is an input: the text states no value except those of section 11.
-- "the annual rate" is defined by section 5(4) ("an amount to be known as the annual rate") and is encoded at section 5(4), 5(5) and 5(6) below.

§ `Section 4 -- Meaning of fee unit`

-- src:53 | If in an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument there is a statement of a number (whether whole, fractional or decimal) of what are called fee units, that statement must, unless the context otherwise requires, be construed as stating a number of dollars equal to the product obtained by multiplying the number of fee units by the amount fixed from time to time by the Treasurer under section 5(3).
@ref s 4 (src:53)
GIVEN `where the statement is made` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4 -- the statement is in an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where the statement is made`
    WHEN `an Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a statutory rule` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a legislative instrument` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an instrument of another kind` THEN FALSE

-- The section opens "If in an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument there is a statement ..." and says the statement "must, unless the context otherwise requires, be construed as stating a number of dollars".
-- Both "If" and "unless" are the text's own conditions: where the statement is in another kind of instrument, or the context otherwise requires, the answer is FALSE.
-- src:53 | If in an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument there is a statement of a number (whether whole, fractional or decimal) of what are called fee units, that statement must, unless the context otherwise requires, be construed as stating a number of dollars equal to the product obtained by multiplying the number of fee units by the amount fixed from time to time by the Treasurer under section 5(3).
@ref s 4 (src:53)
GIVEN `where the statement is made` IS AN Instrument
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4 -- a statement of a number of fee units must be construed as stating dollars` MEANS
        `s 4 -- the statement is in an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument` `where the statement is made`
    AND NOT `the context otherwise requires`

-- Where the section applies and the context does not otherwise require, the dollars are "the product obtained by multiplying the number of fee units
-- by the amount fixed from time to time by the Treasurer under section 5(3)", whole, fractional or decimal, and not rounded.
-- src:53 | If in an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument there is a statement of a number (whether whole, fractional or decimal) of what are called fee units, that statement must, unless the context otherwise requires, be construed as stating a number of dollars equal to the product obtained by multiplying the number of fee units by the amount fixed from time to time by the Treasurer under section 5(3).
@ref s 4 (src:53)
GIVEN `where the statement is made` IS AN Instrument
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of fee units` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 4 -- the number of dollars a statement of fee units states, where the section applies` MEANS
    IF `s 4 -- a statement of a number of fee units must be construed as stating dollars` `where the statement is made` `the context otherwise requires`
    THEN JUST (`s 4 -- the number of dollars a statement of fee units states` `the number of fee units` `the amount fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3)`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 5 -- Calculation of value of fee and penalty units`

-- "The value of a fee unit is the amount fixed with respect to a financial year by the Treasurer by notice published in the Government Gazette."
-- With no such notice the text gives no value, so the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:56 | (1) The value of a fee unit is the amount fixed with respect to a financial year by the Treasurer by notice published in the Government Gazette.
@ref s 5(1) (src:56)
GIVEN `the Treasurer fixed an amount for the financial year by notice published in the Government Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount fixed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 5(1) -- the value of a fee unit for the financial year` MEANS
    IF `the Treasurer fixed an amount for the financial year by notice published in the Government Gazette`
    THEN JUST `the amount fixed`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:57 | (2) The value of a penalty unit is the amount fixed with respect to a financial year by the Treasurer by notice published in the Government Gazette.
@ref s 5(2) (src:57)
GIVEN `the Treasurer fixed an amount for the financial year by notice published in the Government Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount fixed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 5(2) -- the value of a penalty unit for the financial year` MEANS
    IF `the Treasurer fixed an amount for the financial year by notice published in the Government Gazette`
    THEN JUST `the amount fixed`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "The Treasurer may, by notice published in the Government Gazette, fix once each financial year the amounts".
-- The permission is limited in its own wording to a notice in the Gazette and to once a financial year;
-- outside that limit the text says neither yes nor no, so the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:58 | (3) The Treasurer may, by notice published in the Government Gazette, fix once each financial year the amounts referred to in subsections (1) and (2).
@ref s 5(3) (src:58)
GIVEN `the fixing is by notice published in the Government Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of times the amounts were fixed earlier in the financial year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(3) -- the Treasurer may fix the amounts by this notice` MEANS
    IF `the fixing is by notice published in the Government Gazette` AND `the number of times the amounts were fixed earlier in the financial year` EQUALS 0
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "If the Treasurer does not fix an annual rate under subsection (4) for a financial year, the annual rate that was determined for the previous financial year
-- is to be the rate". A rate fixed under subsection (4) is the rate; section 5(4) is in vmu-time (the day before which it is fixed).
-- src:60 | (5) If the Treasurer does not fix an annual rate under subsection (4) for a financial year, the annual rate that was determined for the previous financial year is to be the rate by which the amount of a fee unit or penalty unit is to be adjusted for the financial year.
@ref s 5(5) (src:60)
GIVEN `the annual rate fixed under subsection (4) for the financial year` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the annual rate that was determined for the previous financial year` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 5(5) -- the annual rate for the financial year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the annual rate fixed under subsection (4) for the financial year`
    WHEN JUST rate THEN JUST rate
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the annual rate that was determined for the previous financial year`

-- "must not exceed the amount that is the product ... rounded to the nearest cent": the bar applies when the amount fixed exceeds that amount.
-- The annual rate is a proportion (2⋅5% is 0.025): the amount compared with is the previous value times one plus the rate, rounded to the nearest cent (vmu-time.l4).
-- Where the amount cannot be worked out because the product is exactly half way between two cents, the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:61 | (6) The amount of a fee unit fixed by the Treasurer that is to apply in respect of a financial year must not exceed the amount that is the product of the value of the fee unit in the previous financial year multiplied by the annual rate for the financial year in which the fee unit is to apply rounded to the nearest cent.
@ref s 5(6) (src:61)
GIVEN `the amount of the fee unit fixed by the Treasurer` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the fee unit in the previous financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the annual rate for the financial year in which the fee unit is to apply` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(6) -- the amount of the fee unit fixed exceeds the amount the subsection allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 5(6) -- the product, rounded to the nearest cent` `the value of the fee unit in the previous financial year` `the annual rate for the financial year in which the fee unit is to apply`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST ceiling THEN JUST (`the amount of the fee unit fixed by the Treasurer` GREATER THAN ceiling)

-- src:62 | (7) The amount of a penalty unit fixed by the Treasurer that is to apply in respect of a financial year must not exceed the amount that is the product of the value of the penalty unit in the previous financial year multiplied by the annual rate for the financial year in which the penalty is to apply rounded to the nearest cent.
@ref s 5(7) (src:62)
GIVEN `the amount of the penalty unit fixed by the Treasurer` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of the penalty unit in the previous financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the annual rate for the financial year in which the penalty is to apply` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(7) -- the amount of the penalty unit fixed exceeds the amount the subsection allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 5(7) -- the product, rounded to the nearest cent` `the value of the penalty unit in the previous financial year` `the annual rate for the financial year in which the penalty is to apply`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST ceiling THEN JUST (`the amount of the penalty unit fixed by the Treasurer` GREATER THAN ceiling)

-- "The Treasurer must ensure that the annual rate fixed ... is published on a website maintained by the Department of the Minister administering this Act
-- as soon as practicable after it is fixed." The duty arises once a rate is fixed under subsection (4); before that it has not arisen and the answer is NOTHING.
-- "as soon as practicable" is a judgment the text leaves open, so it is asked as a fact.
-- src:64 | (8) The Treasurer must ensure that the annual rate fixed by the Treasurer under subsection (4) is published on a website maintained by the Department of the Minister administering this Act as soon as practicable after it is fixed.
@ref s 5(8) (src:64)
GIVEN `an annual rate has been fixed under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the rate is published on a website maintained by the Department of the Minister administering this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was published as soon as practicable after it was fixed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5(8) -- the Treasurer has ensured that the annual rate is published` MEANS
    IF `an annual rate has been fixed under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST (`the rate is published on a website maintained by the Department of the Minister administering this Act` AND `it was published as soon as practicable after it was fixed`)
    ELSE NOTHING
